  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nMid level short wave energy will drop down across the southern Great\nLakes this afternoon into tonight. As the airmass across the region \ndestabilizes through this afternoon, scattered showers and \nthunderstorms will develop off to our northwest across parts of \nnorthern Indiana and lower Michigan in association with the short \nwave. This activity will move southeast into at least northwest \nportions of our area by this evening, but the airmass across our \narea will not be as unstable by this time. As a result, expect to \nsee an overall weakening/decreasing trend in coverage as the pcpn \nmoves southeast into our area tonight. Marginal deep layer shear \nwill trend upwards through this evening, so suppose a few strong to \nsevere storms cannot be ruled across mainly our northwest, with \ndamaging wind the main threat. However, this threat should diminish \nfairly quickly as we head into tonight and the pcpn moves southeast \ninto the rest of our area. \n\nThe short wave energy will continue to move east into Thursday. Some\ndestabilization through the afternoon will lead to some additional \nchances for showers and thunderstorms during the afternoon into \nearly evening, primarily across eastern portions of our area.",
